. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         /*      Inclusion/exclusion criteria according to TEAM's PAP: 
>         1. Include individuals >18 years with one child only  [age>18&sumkids
> ==1]
>         2. Exclude homosexuals (who could potentially choose their child's ge
> nder) */
.         
.         *Deviations from PAP
.         *Given that we work with household level observations, we had to slig
> htly adjust the covarites. We use:
.         *years_edu_max: maximum years of education of couple
.         *age_mean_hh: mean of age of couple
.         *age_child, ln_income, syear: same as individual-level regressions  
.         *married and  nationality: we use those from the male respondent in t
> he HH
. 
.         gen sample=(age>18 & sumkids==1 & age_child>0 & heterosexual!=0) // W
> e set age_child>0 because apparently in the 5% data there are "yet to become 
> parents" observations that at the moment of being surveyed have imputed an ag
> e of the child that occurs in the future, so when we build the child's age, i
> t's a negative number. 

.                 
.         
.         /*
>         3. We will append observations from different years and keep only the
>  first time an individual is interviewed (in case a given individual appears 
> more than once)
>            Notice that we define one sample restriction for h2 and h3. for h1
>  and h4 we don't need this as the outcome variable is only available one year
> */
.                 
.                 *For h2
.                         cap drop  n     n_aux filter_year_sample

.                         gsort pid cid syear

.                         bys pid cid  : gen n=_n if leftist!=.
(368,479 missing values generated)

